cted for laboratory studies  throughout the controlled and  uncontrolled areas  schoolchildren from both areas were  brought to the clinic rectal swabs were  made so that bacteriologists could  determine the prevalence of Shigella  organisms epidemiologists determined the  amounts of diarrhea morbidity by going  from house to house through both areas  asking housewives if members of their  families had experience diarrhea in the  last 30 days mortality figures were  obtained from the County Health Officer  in the area to be controlled inspections  were made to find the fly breeding areas  by breeding areas were brought under  control by basic sanitation procedures  this experimental program proved that  dysentery could be reduced from 1/3 to  1/2 by fly control  when we view that dysentery could be  reduced by fly control and the  expenditure of public funds was  justified the next step was to  demonstrate to the state's the proven  operational procedures and train their  personnel in the application of these  practices such arrangements are usually  made through CDC regional  representatives when requests for  assistance come from state health  officers family I wonder if you people  could help us we've got ten counties in  this state where the death and sickness  from dysentery especially babies have  always been higher than the rest of the  state yeah I know  most of those counties are in the  low-income areas no garbage disposal  they had sanitation and pack  everything's bad yes  you know we've always wanted to get some  flak control going down there but we  just haven't had anybody that knows how  to organize the program and I see that  it's carried out we don't have any  equipment trucks bulldozers dragline  sprayers we can send you some big power  sprayers but we have the money for  trucks and draglines and things like  that right now we may be able to give  you a little more help later on in the  meantime could you could you work out a  deal with your highw